  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF &#x2013; Madagascar &#x2013; WASH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an assignment at the request of UNICEF.The Southern regions of Madagascar, Androy, Anosy, Atsimo Andrefana, already the furthest left-behind, are experiencing a humanitarian crisis resulting from recurrent severe drought and food insecurity. Over one million people, over 40% of the population in the 10 most-affected districts &#x2013; are in need of immediate humanitarian assistance.Due to some issues about data collection and data analysis since the beginning of the Drought crisis, the WASH Cluster decided to assess the WASH Cluster Information System. There is urgent need for more coordination of the activities of all stakeholders providing emergency WASH services to the affected populations. The WASH sector needs to increase it Information Management (IM) skills set and experience, to be able to respond to high reporting demand. The IM WASH expert will assist on improving data management within the wash cluster in Madagascar.</narrative>
  </description>
